<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<policyDefinitionResources revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0">
    <displayName/>
    <description/>
    <resources>

<stringTable>
<string id="SUPPORTED_WINXPSP2">Microsoft Windows XP SP2 or later</string>
<string id="ietab">IE Tab</string>
<string id="EndUserControlGroup">User Lockdown</string>
<string id="LicenseGroup">License (Required)</string>
<string id="GeneralSettings">Settings</string>

<string id="LicenseeName">Licensee Name</string>
<string id="LicenseeName_Explain">
This is the "Licensee Name" that is associated with the IE Tab license.

You must supply valid license information for the Group Policy features to work. Learn more about IE Tab licensing here:

http://www.ietab.net/license

</string>

<string id="LicenseKey">License Key</string>
<string id="LicenseKey_Explain">
This is the "License Key" that is associated with the IE Tab license.

You must supply valid license information for the Group Policy features to work. Learn more about IE Tab licensing here:

http://www.ietab.net/license
</string>

<string id="AutoURLFile">Auto URL file location</string>
<string id="AutoURLFile_Explain">
Supply a URL that points to a file that has a list of additional Auto URLs to use.  May be a file:// or http:// URL.

The file format is simple:  One Auto URL per line.  Auto URL exceptions may be supplied in the file by prefixing the line with x/, as in x/*ietab.net*

These Auto URLs are appended to the list of other Auto URLs that have been supplied by group policy.

</string>

<string id="AllowChangeAutoURLs">Allow Change: List of Auto URLs</string>
<string id="AllowChangeAutoURLs_Explain">
If you enable this setting, users can change the set of Auto URLs.  If administrative URLs are supplied, the user's Auto URLs will override them.

If you disable this setting, users cannot change the set of Auto URLs and only the administrative Auto URLs will apply.

If this setting is not set, users can change the set of Auto URLs and override the administrative Auto URLs.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeAutoURLExceptions">Allow Change: Auto URL Exceptions</string>
<string id="AllowChangeAutoURLExceptions_Explain">
If you enable this setting, users can change the set of Auto URL exceptions.  If administrative URL exceptions are supplied, the user's Auto URL exceptions will override them.

If you disable this setting, users cannot change the set of Auto URL exceptions and only the administrative Auto URL exceptions will apply.

If this setting is not enabled or disabled, users can change the set of Auto URL exceptions and override the administrative Auto URLs.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeEnableAutoURLs">Allow Change: Enable Auto URLs</string>
<string id="AllowChangeEnableAutoURLs_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Enable Auto URLs" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeCookieSync">Allow Change: Enable cookie sync</string>
<string id="AllowChangeCookieSync_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Enable cookie sync" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeSessionShare">Allow Change: Enable session sharing between tabs</string>
<string id="AllowChangeSessionShare_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Enable session sharing between tabs" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>


<string id="AllowChangeFavicon">Allow Change: Replace IE Tab icon with current site icon</string>
<string id="AllowChangeFavicon_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Replace IE Tab icon with current site icon" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeBeforeUnload">Allow Change: Enable beforeunload checking</string>
<string id="AllowChangeBeforeUnload_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Enable beforeunload checking" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>

<string id="AllowChangeEnableDirectInvoke">Allow Change: Enable DirectInvoke</string>
<string id="AllowChangeEnableDirectInvoke_Explain">
If you enable this setting, the end-user can change the "Enable Direct Invoke" setting.

If you disable this setting, the user can not change the setting.  By default the user CAN change the setting.
</string>

